---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../../../components/Section.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import DocTable from '../../../components/DocTable.astro';
import DocNote from '../../../components/DocNote.astro';
import { pluginDocs } from '../../../data/site';

const next = pluginDocs[1];
---

<Base
  title="Plugin authoring — modplayjs"
  description="The five modplayjs plugin contracts, the load/row/tick call chain, registration order and the core time model."
  layout="docs"
>
  <div class="breadcrumbs py-0 font-mono text-[0.64rem] text-base-content/30">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/api" class="hover:text-primary">Library API</a></li>
      <li class="text-base-content/50">Plugin authoring</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <header class="mt-3 border-b border-base-300 pb-8">
    <p class="font-mono text-[0.64rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-base-content/35">
      Plugin authoring / 00
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Plugins</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-[0.96rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/65">
      Everything outside the core is a plugin. A plugin is a plain object with a
      <span class="font-mono text-[0.86rem]">name</span> and one of five contracts; you register it, the core calls it.
      There is no lifecycle wrapper, no decorator and no build step.
    </p>
  </header>

  <Section index="01" title="Five contracts" note="one registry each">
    <DocTable
      columns={['Kind', 'Contract', 'Register with', 'Chosen by']}
      rows={[
        ['Format', 'FormatPlugin', 'registries.registerFormat(p)', 'test() probe order'],
        ['Effect', 'EffectPlugin', 'registries.registerEffect(p)', 'registration order'],
        ['DSP', 'DspPlugin', 'registries.registerDsp(p)', 'core.setDsp(name)'],
        ['Output', 'OutputPlugin', 'registries.registerOutput(p)', 'the host app'],
        ['Export', 'ExportPlugin', 'registries.registerExport(p)', 'the studio / UI'],
      ]}
    />
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[74ch] text-[0.86rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/55">
      A format plugin and a DSP are the two you need for playback. Effects are optional observers that see every
      channel after the format reader. Outputs are the pull side. Exports are the write side of a format loader.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section index="02" title="The call chain" note="load → row → tick → pull">
    <DocTable
      columns={['Stage', 'Call', 'What runs']}
      rows={[
        ['Load', 'core.loadModule(bytes)', 'Depack PP20/ICE, probe every FormatPlugin.test() in order, call the first match’s load(), then finalize (sequence scan, envelope clamps, instrument keys).'],
        ['Start', 'core.startPlayer()', 'State LOADED → PLAYING. The DSP’s reset() runs on start.'],
        ['Row', 'per channel', 'format.readEvent(core, chn, row), then every EffectPlugin.onRow, then every DspPlugin.onRow.'],
        ['Tick', 'per channel', 'Every EffectPlugin.onTick; after processTick, every EffectPlugin.onTickPost.'],
        ['Render', 'per tick', 'DspPlugin.renderFrame(core, out, ticks) fills ticks × ticksize × 2 interleaved floats.'],
        ['Pull', 'core.playBuffer(out, size, loop)', 'Whole ticks are copied into the caller’s buffer. The output decides when to call.'],
      ]}
    />
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[74ch] text-[0.86rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/55">
      The format reader is re-entered through the registry on every row: <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">core.registries.format(mod.format).readEvent(...)</span>.
      That is why <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">ModuleData.format</span> must equal the plugin’s
      <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">name</span>.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section index="03" title="The clock" note="one formula for every format">
    <p class="max-w-[72ch] text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/60">
      One tick is <span class="font-mono text-[0.82rem]">ticksize</span> samples. The core recomputes it every tick,
      so a tempo change takes effect on the current row. The formula is libxmp’s, with truncation, not rounding:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      title="ticksize"
      lang="formula"
      code={`ticksize = (int)(sampleRate × time_factor × rrate / bpm / 1000)

defaults: time_factor = 10, rrate = 250
        = (int)(sampleRate × 2.5 / bpm)

44,100 Hz, 125 BPM → 882 samples = 20 ms
a row lasts speed ticks (speed 6 = 120 ms)`}
    />
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[72ch] text-[0.86rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/55">
      A DSP never computes time from wall clocks. <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">renderFrame</span> is given
      <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">ticks</span> and reads <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">core.ticksize</span>
      for the current value.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section index="04" title="Registration rules" note="names are keys">
    <ul class="max-w-[74ch] space-y-2 text-[0.88rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/60">
      <li>
        Names are unique per kind. Registering the same name twice throws
        <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">PluginNotFoundError</span>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Format probing stops at the first <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">test()</span> that returns true.
        Register the narrow/signature formats before broad ones, or accept that order decides.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">test()</span> must be cheap and must not throw on short input.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">core.setDsp(name)</span> only works while the player is stopped;
        it throws <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">StateError</span> while playing.
      </li>
      <li>
        The core does not start an output. The host app creates/pulls it; the studio and the demo do this in their
        own click handler.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section index="05" title="Errors" note="one family">
    <p class="max-w-[72ch] text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/60">
      Every error extends <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">ModplayError</span>, so one catch block handles the family:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      title="Error classes"
      code={`ModplayError            base
UnknownFormatError      no registered plugin accepted the bytes
ParseError              a loader found a bad header / truncated data
PackedModuleError       packed wrapper with no depacker
StateError              wrong lifecycle order (start before load, setDsp while playing)
PluginNotFoundError     unknown name, duplicate registration
SampleError             unknown sample id, empty or oversized swap`}
    />
  </Section>

  <Section index="06" title="Read next" note="five contracts">
    <div class="grid gap-px border border-base-300 bg-base-300 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        pluginDocs.slice(1).map((doc) => (
          <a href={`/api/plugins/${doc.slug}`} class="group bg-base-100 p-4 hover:bg-base-200/60">
            <p class="font-mono text-[0.6rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-base-content/30">{doc.order}</p>
            <h3 class="mt-1 text-[0.95rem] font-semibold group-hover:text-primary">{doc.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-1 text-[0.8rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/50">{doc.blurb}</p>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <DocNote>
      The contracts below are the same ones the shipped loaders, mixers and outputs implement. Nothing on these
      pages is an example-only interface.
    </DocNote>
  </Section>

  <nav class="mt-16 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 border-t border-base-300 pt-5">
    <a href="/api" class="font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-base-content/35 hover:text-primary">
      ← Library API
    </a>
    <a
      href={`/api/plugins/${next.slug}`}
      class="text-right font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-base-content/50 hover:text-primary"
    >
      {next.order} · {next.title} →
    </a>
  </nav>
</Base>
